\begin{lemma}[Tails over topological types]\label{lem:tails}
Fix $M_0>0$. There are $C_{M_0},B_{M_0}$ such that, for all sufficiently
large $h$ and all $1\le p\le M_0\sqrt h$,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 S_{g,p}^{[L]}&\le C_{M_0}\left(\frac{B_{M_0}(p+L)}h\right)^L,
                  &&2\le L\le\sqrt h,\\
 T_{g,p}^{[L]}&\le C_{M_0}\left(\frac{B_{M_0}(p+L)}h\right)^L,
                  &&1\le L\le\sqrt h,
 \end{aligned}
 \label{eq:FE13}
\end{equation}
the second bound being used only for $p\ge2$. The ranges of $L$ start at
the stability minima two and one respectively.
